Root cause:
The bug was caused by the premature release of cached dentries during the `cifs_kill_sb` function, which could be invoked even when the filesystem mount had failed. This led to attempts to dereference and release dentries that were not valid, resulting in potential memory management issues. The fix ensures that cached dentries are only released if the filesystem mount is complete, indicated by the presence of a populated `cifs_sb->root`.
